# i18n

Locales: `pt-BR` (default, `https://www.guilhermeguain.com.br`) and `en` (`/en`). Detection is off. The language selector navigates to `/` or `/en`. `src/proxy.ts` rewrites `/` to the `pt-BR` segment.

- One JSON file per namespace under `public/locales/{locale}/`.
- Namespaces: `common`, `meta`, `menu`, `hero`, `about`, `hard-skills`, `soft-skills`, `data-driven-seo`, `front-end-ai`, `experience`, `projects`, `education`, `events`.
- Always add/change keys in **both** `en` and `pt-BR`. Keep key trees identical.
- Nested objects are fine (`experience.ifood.role`). Components read them as `t('experience:ifood.role')`.
- New namespace: create both JSON files **and** register the name in `src/lib/i18n.ts`.
- Do not put user-facing copy in hooks or JSX when it belongs in locale JSON. Tech badge titles (`React.js`) may stay in code.
